{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mummy-the-curse/377578-discovering-a-true-name","id":377578,"title":"Discovering a True Name?","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Mummy: The Curse"],"posts":[{"date":"2015-01-21T16:07:05-08:00","id":377578,"title":"Discovering a True Name?","content":"With how much Book of the Deceived leans on True Names as a mechanic, it seems a rather glaring omission to have no system for finding them out. Am I missing something or are we forced to use homebrew (and if so, what would you use for the process?)<br /> <br /> I'm considering an extended Intelligence+Occult roll with penalties if the target isn't in front of you, but that seems a little lame.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Remi. she/her. game designer.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/281-atamajakki","name":"atamajakki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar281_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5487"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-01-21T16:20:34-08:00","id":377593,"title":"","content":"We've been told a few times that &quot;something&quot; is coming expanding on stuff in Deceived. Determining a True Name is meant to be part of it.<br /> <br /> Personally, I told my players that it would be a long (session-ish for mortal, probably a bit longer for longer-lived supernatural creatures) process involving multiple Intelligence + Academics rolls. The description of True Names makes them out to be every name the individual has ever been called, strung together. I feel that puts it more in Academic territory than Occult, although an Occult roll may be necessary to string them together to form the appropriate sounds.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1059-azahul","name":"Azahul","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1465"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-01-21T17:47:16-08:00","id":377633,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Azahul</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mummy-the-curse/377578-discovering-a-true-name?p=377593#post377593\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">We've been told a few times that &quot;something&quot; is coming expanding on stuff in Deceived. Determining a True Name is meant to be part of it.<br /> <br /> Personally, I told my players that it would be a long (session-ish for mortal, probably a bit longer for longer-lived supernatural creatures) process involving multiple Intelligence + Academics rolls. The description of True Names makes them out to be every name the individual has ever been called, strung together. I feel that puts it more in Academic territory than Occult, although an Occult roll may be necessary to string them together to form the appropriate sounds.</div> </div> </div> </div>Honestly depends on the subject. Intel+academics may help out with other Arisen or mortals in academia, it creates an problem when your dealing with informal networks such as criminal groups and the underworld in general.<br /> <br /> Not to mention the collection of usernames a person may use during their online existence.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/604-shock","name":"Shock","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar604_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1071"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-01-25T17:04:53-08:00","id":381441,"title":"","content":"It is mentioned somewhere in one of the Mummy books that a True Name is composed of: a person's birth name, every other name and title they go by, and a set of mystical syllabes that describe her connection to the universe. If I recall correctly.<br /> <br /> Ah, here we go, it's in Guildhalls Of The Deathless, mentioned in the description of the Redacting The Word Tier 3 effect. Didn't remember it with the greatest accuracy.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Guildhalls Of The Deathless, Page 115</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">A typical mortal\u2019s true name includes her full legal name, all nicknames (even the most private), and a sequence of mystical syllables that describe her unique connection to the cosmos.</div> </div> </div> </div>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":188,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/188-yeoflittlefaith","user":"YeOfLittleFaith","date":". 01-25-2015, 08:11 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/188-yeoflittlefaith","name":"YeOfLittleFaith","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar188_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1159"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-01-25T20:01:00-08:00","id":381542,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>YeOfLittleFaith</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mummy-the-curse/377578-discovering-a-true-name?p=381441#post381441\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It is mentioned somewhere in one of the Mummy books that a True Name is composed of: a person's birth name, every other name and title they go by, and a set of mystical syllabes that describe her connection to the universe. If I recall correctly.<br /> <br /> Ah, here we go, it's in Guildhalls Of The Deathless, mentioned in the description of the Redacting The Word Tier 3 effect. Didn't remember it with the greatest accuracy.<br /> <br /></div> </div> </div> </div>Jesus, modern True Names must be a pain the ass. Think of all the usernames involved!","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Remi. she/her. game designer.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/281-atamajakki","name":"atamajakki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar281_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5487"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-01-25T20:35:45-08:00","id":381556,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>atamajakki</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mummy-the-curse/377578-discovering-a-true-name?p=381542#post381542\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Jesus, modern True Names must be a pain the ass. Think of all the usernames involved!</div> </div> </div> </div>Makes me thinks that Cults either outsource or have competent Doxxers on staff/retainer.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/604-shock","name":"Shock","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar604_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1071"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-01-25T21:44:06-08:00","id":381607,"title":"","content":"...I've just realized something. The Arisen obsession with lofty titles is really just a means of further complicating their True Names! Not that it matters, of course, what with the whole &quot;names kept hidden by the Judges&quot; thing.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Remi. she/her. game designer.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/281-atamajakki","name":"atamajakki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar281_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5487"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-01-25T23:37:08-08:00","id":381633,"title":"","content":"Book of the Deceived actually brought up the title thing. A title has no mystical connection to its bearer. If your minions only know you as &quot;The Hand of Wisdom&quot;, it gives you a shield between any enemies who might wish to wield Name Magic against you. A title like that simply can't be used by a wielder of Name Magic to target its owner.<br /> <br /> I wonder, in the case of the Deceived themselves, whether the names of their Temakh make up part of their own True Names?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1059-azahul","name":"Azahul","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1465"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-26T10:23:54-08:00","id":420415,"title":"","content":"And now your questions are answered.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4248-nephilpal","name":"Nephilpal","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4248_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"79"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-26T10:51:24-08:00","id":420445,"title":"","content":"It seemed to me that a True Name was like a platonic ideal that didn't really come into play that very often at all. You never directly interact with it, but you do interact with lesser reflections and representations of it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3386-piff","name":"Piff","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3386_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"442"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-27T16:19:26-08:00","id":422282,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Piff</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mummy-the-curse/377578-discovering-a-true-name?p=420445#post420445\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It seemed to me that a True Name was like a platonic ideal that didn't really come into play that very often at all. You never directly interact with it, but you do interact with lesser reflections and representations of it.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Precisely so.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4248-nephilpal","name":"Nephilpal","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4248_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"79"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-27T16:39:51-08:00","id":422304,"title":"","content":"For those who didn't get the signpost, it can now be found in Lore of the Deceived, which in turn can be found at the link below.<br /> <br /> Edit: <a href=\"http://rpg.drivethrustuff.com/product/144748/Lore-of-the-Deceived\" target=\"_blank\">http://rpg.drivethrustuff.com/produc...f-the-Deceived</a>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Thoughts ripple out, birthing others","edited":{"userid":1624,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1624-falleneco","user":"FallenEco","date":".  link problems 02-27-2015, 07:41 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1624-falleneco","name":"FallenEco","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1624_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1927"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-01T09:15:18-08:00","id":424207,"title":"","content":"Hmm. Could knowledge of a True Name be applied to the abilities of other creatures? <b>Changeling</b> and <b>Mage</b>, at least, have already given some applications to knowing a subject's name, so what might a True Name allow them to do?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":665,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/665-shkspr1048","user":"shkspr1048","date":". 03-01-2015, 12:19 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/665-shkspr1048","name":"shkspr1048","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"630"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-01T09:30:18-08:00","id":424215,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>shkspr1048</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mummy-the-curse/377578-discovering-a-true-name?p=424207#post424207\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Hmm. Could knowledge of a True Name be applied to the abilities of other creatures? <b>Changeling</b> and <b>Mage</b>, at least, have already given some applications to knowing a subject's name, so what might a True Name allow them to do?</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> The answer is a bit complicated. Mage defines true names differently than mummy, with each game using the definition most appropriate to the line's themes. If I recall correctly, Mage's take is more of a self-defined appellation, while mummy is a more holistic set of descriptors that come together to make a unified symbol. That said, the system I put in Lore of the Deceived is deliberately intended to be something anyone can figure out. Thus, if you wanted to run with the mummy approach and then design capabilities for other critters that keyed off that, more power to you.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4248-nephilpal","name":"Nephilpal","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4248_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"79"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-01T17:58:57-08:00","id":424716,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Nephilpal</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mummy-the-curse/377578-discovering-a-true-name?p=424215#post424215\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> The answer is a bit complicated. Mage defines true names differently than mummy, with each game using the definition most appropriate to the line's themes. If I recall correctly, Mage's take is more of a self-defined appellation, while mummy is a more holistic set of descriptors that come together to make a unified symbol. That said, the system I put in Lore of the Deceived is deliberately intended to be something anyone can figure out. Thus, if you wanted to run with the mummy approach and then design capabilities for other critters that keyed off that, more power to you.</div> </div> </div> </div>Actually, in Mummy, a true name is an equation that describes, in occult fashion, what a being in at the very present. In Mage, a true name is your birth name or the name you think of as being &quot;you.&quot;<br /> <br /> Former's more complex and beautiful than the other, but the latter is also a hell of a lot more useful on a regular basis.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.us/a/img824/1346/mosz.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/180-leliel","name":"Leliel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar180_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2259"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-01T18:07:25-08:00","id":424721,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Nephilpal</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mummy-the-curse/377578-discovering-a-true-name?p=424215#post424215\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Mage defines true names differently than mummy, with each game using the definition most appropriate to the line's themes. If I recall correctly, Mage's take is more of a self-defined appellation</div> </div> </div> </div>Lel's got the right of it; you're thinking of Shadow Names. The capital-T True Names of Mage are the stuff of sympathy-scrambling archmagic.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-01T18:39:15-08:00","id":424738,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Leliel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mummy-the-curse/377578-discovering-a-true-name?p=424716#post424716\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Actually, in Mummy, a true name is an equation that describes, in occult fashion, what a being in at the very present. In Mage, a true name is your birth name or the name you think of as being &quot;you.&quot;<br /> <br /> Former's more complex and beautiful than the other, but the latter is also a hell of a lot more useful on a regular basis.</div> </div> </div> </div>You know, the distinction makes a certain amount of sense, when you lay them next to each-other.<br /> <br /> Mages have access (however limited) to the Root of All Meaning (i.e. the Supernal). Their magic boils down to directly futzing with meaning, bypassing any magical laws of &quot;physics&quot; that might exist in the Fallen World.<br /> <br /> Mummies brute-force their way through those same laws in a way that reflects their glorious might.<br /> <br /> It's like the difference between using a GUI (Mage) and using the terminal (Mummy); both get you the same places, it's just that certain things are harder when you do them different ways.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I have decided, after some thought, that I don't really feel happy on these forums. I might decide to come back to post. Who knows - but right now, I'm gone.<br /> <br /> So good bye, good luck, and have a nice day.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1170-amechra","name":"amechra","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1170_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2316"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}